\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Conjugation on one direction}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Choose one Euclidean direction. On the spin space in
\ref{fdip-016Q} its action exchanges two real basis vectors.
The line spanned by their sum has direction eigenvalue #{1},
and the line spanned by their difference has eigenvalue #{-1}.
If only the first line is kept as the whole spin space, where
could a conjugation that negates the direction send its vectors?}
